IMPORT prelude

-- Registration of Births and Deaths Act 2021 (Singapore) -- who must report a birth, death or stillbirth, to whom, and the
-- deadlines and penalties that follow (ss 7, 8, 10, 22, 23, 26, 32, 33, 35); what counts as a stillborn child (s 2(1)); the rules on
-- a child's name in the register (ss 19, 20, 21); registering a death abroad (s 28); and the false-statement offence (s 48).
--
-- Edition: Act 17 of 2021 (not a 2020 Revised Edition -- the Act post-dates it), informal consolidation, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/RBDA2021.txt ("version in force from 30/9/2026"), with amendments by Act 2 of 2024 (in force
-- 16 April 2024), Act 20 of 2022 (in force 15 October 2024) and Act 16 of 2026 (in force 30 September 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duties that fall on parents,
-- relatives, occupiers, doctors, hospitals and masters of conveyances, and on naming a child. Not encoded: administration and
-- delegation (ss 3-6), registration of births in conveyances (ss 11-13), adoption, legitimation and assisted-reproduction
-- re-registration (ss 14-18), registration duties of the Registrar-General (ss 9, 24, 25, 29, 30, 34, 36), registers and
-- corrections (ss 37-41), information and investigation powers (ss 42-47) beyond their penalties, register and certificate
-- offences (ss 49-50A), corporate liability, composition, and Parts 9-10.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Registration of Births and Deaths Act 2021 -- reporting`

DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `in a hospital`
    `in other premises`
    `in a conveyance in Singapore`
    `in any other place`

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a parent`
    `a legal guardian`
    `a doctor attending at the hospital`
    `the hospital`
    `an occupier who knows`
    `the master of the conveyance`
    `a relative present at the event`
    `a relative who knows but was absent`
    `a bystander present at the event`
    `a person who took charge of the body`

§§ `7 -- report of a birth in Singapore`

-- s 7(2): responsible for reporting: (a) born in a hospital -- "every medical practitioner who attends to the birth, and the
-- hospital"; (b) born outside a hospital "and is brought to a hospital within 24 hours after the child's birth" -- every doctor who
-- attends to the child at the hospital, and the hospital; (c) born in other premises -- "the child's parents, and every occupier of
-- the premises who knows of the child's birth"; (d) in a conveyance in Singapore -- the parents and the master; (e) any other place
-- -- the parents. (3): the people in (c), (d), (e) remain responsible even if the child is brought to a hospital within 24 hours.
-- (4): report to the Registrar-General "as soon as practicable"; (5): one report discharges everyone; (6): without reasonable
-- excuse, $1,500 or one month or both.
--
-- For a birth IN a hospital the parents are not on the list.
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `the person` IS A Person, `brought to hospital within 24 hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `responsible for reporting the birth` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `in a hospital` THEN `is hospital staff` `the person`
    WHEN `in other premises` THEN
            `the person` EQUALS `a parent`
        OR  `the person` EQUALS `an occupier who knows`
        OR  (`brought to hospital within 24 hours` AND `is hospital staff` `the person`)
    WHEN `in a conveyance in Singapore` THEN
            `the person` EQUALS `a parent`
        OR  `the person` EQUALS `the master of the conveyance`
        OR  (`brought to hospital within 24 hours` AND `is hospital staff` `the person`)
    OTHERWISE
            `the person` EQUALS `a parent`
        OR  (`brought to hospital within 24 hours` AND `is hospital staff` `the person`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is hospital staff` IF
        `the person` EQUALS `a doctor attending at the hospital`
    OR  `the person` EQUALS `the hospital`

-- The same offence shape recurs in ss 7(6), 10(6), 22(5), 26(5), 32(5), 35(5): a responsible person, no report by ANY
-- responsible person (one report discharges all), and no reasonable excuse. Unlike s 5 of the Coroners Act 2010, the Act does not
-- say who bears the burden of proving the excuse.
GIVEN `is responsible` IS A BOOLEAN, `someone reported` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to report is an offence` IF
    `is responsible` AND (NOT `someone reported`) AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `8 -- birth particulars within 42 days`

-- s 8(5): "responsible person" here means every parent, a legal guardian, or (for certain CYPA orders) the Director-General of
-- Social Welfare or a protector -- NOT the doctor or hospital who reported the birth under s 7. (1)(a): provide the birth
-- particulars "within 42 days after the child's birth". (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply in the case of a child who dies
-- within 42 days after the child's birth." (3): one person's compliance discharges the rest. (4): $1,500 or one month or both,
-- and "a further fine not exceeding $50 for every day" the offence continues after conviction.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must provide the birth particulars` IF
        `the person` EQUALS `a parent`
    OR  `the person` EQUALS `a legal guardian`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `days since the birth` IS A NUMBER, `the child died within 42 days` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `particulars provided by anyone` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in breach of the 42-day duty` IF
        `must provide the birth particulars` `the person`
    AND `days since the birth` GREATER THAN 42
    AND (NOT `the child died within 42 days`)
    AND (NOT `particulars provided by anyone`)
    AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`)

-- s 8(1A)(a) (Act 2 of 2024): where the birth is registered without a name, the duty to provide the name "continues despite the
-- registration until the end of 7 years after the child's birth".
GIVEN `registered without a name` IS A BOOLEAN, `name provided` IS A BOOLEAN, `whole years since the birth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty to provide the name continues` IF
    `registered without a name` AND (NOT `name provided`) AND `whole years since the birth` LESS THAN 7

§§ `19, 20, 21 -- the child's name`

-- s 19(1): the name "(a) must be in a form expressed in characters in the modern English alphabet; (b) may include a permitted
-- character; and (c) must not exceed the number of characters permitted in the electronic form of the register". The limit is
-- not stated in the Act; it is an input here.
GIVEN `only English letters or permitted characters` IS A BOOLEAN, `length of the name` IS A NUMBER, `register limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name is in an acceptable form` IF
    `only English letters or permitted characters` AND `length of the name` AT MOST `register limit`

-- s 19(2): the Registrar-General MAY refuse a name that "(a) contains anything that represents or resembles a title, a rank or an
-- award"; (b) in a patronymic or matronymic system, uses an expression "that does not correspond to the child's sex"; (c) "is
-- obscene or offensive"; or (d) "is contrary to the public interest".
GIVEN `resembles a title, rank or award` IS A BOOLEAN, `lineage marker does not match sex` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obscene or offensive` IS A BOOLEAN, `contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name may be refused` IF
        `resembles a title, rank or award`
    OR  `lineage marker does not match sex`
    OR  `obscene or offensive`
    OR  `contrary to the public interest`

-- s 20: where a birth is registered without a name, a responsible person may apply for a name to be entered, "within 7 years after
-- the child's birth"; the Registrar-General may enter it if the name complies with s 19(1) and is not refused under s 19(2).
GIVEN `registered without a name` IS A BOOLEAN, `whole years since the birth` IS A NUMBER, `name acceptable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `name refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late name may be entered` IF
    `registered without a name` AND `whole years since the birth` LESS THAN 7 AND `name acceptable` AND (NOT `name refused`)

-- s 21: where a name was entered at registration, a responsible person may apply to alter it "within one year after the child's
-- birth"; the Registrar-General may alter it if (b) the new name complies and is not refused, (c) the name "has not been altered
-- before under this section", and (d) "the child is not deceased". A name may be changed under s 21 ONCE.
GIVEN `name entered at registration` IS A BOOLEAN, `whole months since the birth` IS A NUMBER, `name acceptable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `name refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `altered before` IS A BOOLEAN, `the child is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name may be altered` IF
        `name entered at registration`
    AND `whole months since the birth` LESS THAN 12
    AND `name acceptable`
    AND (NOT `name refused`)
    AND (NOT `altered before`)
    AND (NOT `the child is deceased`)

§§ `22, 32 -- report of a death or stillbirth in Singapore`

-- s 22(1): a death in Singapore must be reported under this section "if the death is not, or does not appear to be, a reportable
-- death" (reportable deaths go to the police under the Coroners Act 2010; s 31 preserves duties under other written law).
-- (2): (a) in a hospital -- the hospital; (b) other premises -- "every relative of the deceased person who is present at the death"
-- and every occupier who knows; (c) conveyance in Singapore -- every relative "in the conveyance at the time and knows of the
-- death", and the master; (d) any other place -- every relative who knows, every person present, and every person who takes charge
-- of the body. (3): report "to a medical practitioner" as soon as practicable. (5): $1,500 or one month or both.
-- s 32(2) repeats the same list word for word for a stillbirth (relatives "of the stillborn child"), and s 32(3) the same duty.
-- (Being in the conveyance at the time is treated here as being present.)
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `responsible for reporting the death` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `in a hospital` THEN `the person` EQUALS `the hospital`
    WHEN `in other premises` THEN
            `the person` EQUALS `a relative present at the event`
        OR  `the person` EQUALS `an occupier who knows`
    WHEN `in a conveyance in Singapore` THEN
            `the person` EQUALS `a relative present at the event`
        OR  `the person` EQUALS `the master of the conveyance`
    OTHERWISE
            `the person` EQUALS `a relative present at the event`
        OR  `the person` EQUALS `a relative who knows but was absent`
        OR  `the person` EQUALS `a bystander present at the event`
        OR  `the person` EQUALS `a person who took charge of the body`

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place, `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `responsible for reporting the stillbirth` IF
    `responsible for reporting the death` `the place` `the person`

GIVEN `apparently a reportable death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 22 applies` IF NOT `apparently a reportable death`

-- s 2(1) "stillborn child": a child that "(a) issues from the child's mother after the twenty-fourth week of pregnancy; and (b) does
-- not show any sign of life at any time after being completely expelled or extracted", and "does not include a foetus that is
-- aborted by or through treatment carried out for termination of pregnancy". READING: "after the twenty-fourth week" is taken as
-- 24 or more completed weeks.
GIVEN `completed weeks of pregnancy` IS A NUMBER, `showed a sign of life` IS A BOOLEAN, `a termination of pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is stillborn` IF
    `completed weeks of pregnancy` AT LEAST 24 AND (NOT `showed a sign of life`) AND (NOT `a termination of pregnancy`)

§§ `7, 10, 22, 26, 32, 35 -- to whom the report goes`

-- s 7(4), 10(4): births go to the Registrar-General. s 22(3), 32(3): deaths and stillbirths in Singapore go to "a medical
-- practitioner", who then has 24 hours to send particulars to the Registrar-General (ss 23(2), 33(1)(b)). s 26(3), 35(3): a death
-- or stillbirth in a conveyance outside but bound for Singapore goes "to the police".
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `a birth in Singapore`
    `a birth on a conveyance bound for Singapore`
    `a non-reportable death in Singapore`
    `a death on a conveyance bound for Singapore`
    `a stillbirth in Singapore`
    `a stillbirth on a conveyance bound for Singapore`

DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the Registrar-General`
    `a medical practitioner`
    `the police`

GIVEN `the event` IS A Event
GIVETH A Recipient
`the report goes to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `a birth in Singapore` THEN `the Registrar-General`
    WHEN `a birth on a conveyance bound for Singapore` THEN `the Registrar-General`
    WHEN `a non-reportable death in Singapore` THEN `a medical practitioner`
    WHEN `a stillbirth in Singapore` THEN `a medical practitioner`
    OTHERWISE `the police`

-- s 10(1), 26(1), 35(1): an event in a conveyance outside Singapore must be reported only if it happened during the flight,
-- voyage or passage TO Singapore, and the child or body "arrives in Singapore" and "was not taken to any foreign country or
-- territory" in between.
GIVEN `during the journey to Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `arrived in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `taken to a foreign country first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance event must be reported` IF
    `during the journey to Singapore` AND `arrived in Singapore` AND (NOT `taken to a foreign country first`)

§§ `28 -- death of a citizen or PR abroad`

-- s 28(1): where a Singapore citizen or PR dies outside Singapore "and the body of the deceased person is brought to Singapore", a
-- relative may apply. (2)(a) within 3 months; (b) with a document from a medical practitioner "whether in Singapore or elsewhere"
-- certifying the cause of death. (5): not for a death required to be reported under s 26.
GIVEN `citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN, `body brought to Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `a section 26 death` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `whole months since the death` IS A NUMBER, `has a cause-of-death certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a relative may apply under section 28` IF
        `citizen or permanent resident`
    AND `body brought to Singapore`
    AND (NOT `a section 26 death`)
    AND `whole months since the death` LESS THAN 3
    AND `has a cause-of-death certificate`

§§ `48 -- false or misleading statements`

-- s 48: a statement to the Registrar-General "false or misleading in a material particular", made "(a) knowing it to be false or
-- misleading" or "(b) being reckless as to whether it is", is an offence: $10,000 or 10 years or both.
GIVEN `false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew` IS A BOOLEAN, `reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement is an offence` IF
    `false in a material particular` AND (`knew` OR `reckless`)

§§ `Penalties`

-- ss 7(6), 10(6), 22(5), 26(5), 32(5), 35(5): $1,500 or one month. s 8(4): $1,500 or one month (plus $50 a day continuing).
-- ss 23(3), 33(2): a doctor who fails to send particulars within 24 hours: fine up to $1,000, no imprisonment. s 42(3): failing
-- to answer an information notice: $1,500 or one month. s 48: $10,000 or 10 years. s 51: obstruction, $2,500 or 3 months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to report a birth, death or stillbirth`
    `failing to provide birth particulars`
    `a doctor failing to send particulars within 24 hours`
    `ignoring an information notice`
    `a false or misleading statement`
    `obstruction`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to report a birth, death or stillbirth` THEN 1500
    WHEN `failing to provide birth particulars` THEN 1500
    WHEN `a doctor failing to send particulars within 24 hours` THEN 1000
    WHEN `ignoring an information notice` THEN 1500
    WHEN `a false or misleading statement` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 2500

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to report a birth, death or stillbirth` THEN 1
    WHEN `failing to provide birth particulars` THEN 1
    WHEN `a doctor failing to send particulars within 24 hours` THEN 0
    WHEN `ignoring an information notice` THEN 1
    WHEN `a false or misleading statement` THEN 120
    OTHERWISE 3
